ove because:\n- It develops a piece toward the center\n- It controls key central squares (d4, e5)\n- It prepares for kingside castling\n- It's flexible and doesn't commit to a specific pawn structure yet\n- It follows opening principles: develop knights before bishops, control the center\n- This move fits well with almost any subsequent plan White might choose\n\nAnswer: N: g1-f3"}
