ore fundamental - it secures the center immediately and opens the diagonal for my c1 bishop.\n\nReason: Playing d2-d4 establishes a powerful pawn center with pawns on e4 and d4, controlling key central squares (d5, e5). This classical setup gives White maximum space advantage, opens the c1-h6 diagonal for my light-squared bishop, and maintains flexibility for piece development. This is more important than premature piece moves at this stage.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4"}
