n this hopeless position, White's only practical chance is to push pawns aggressively toward promotion. The b4 advance creates a potential passed pawn on the queenside, which is White's best hope for counterplay. Passive King moves accomplish nothing when facing such overwhelming material deficit.\n\nAnswer: P: b2-b4"}
